sally a little boy died earlier this  week in a shooting police call  preventable  this tragic situation has sparked a new  conversation regarding gun safety  8 news 9 reporter madison kimbrough went  to a local gun range today  she joins us live in the newsroom with  some important safety tips madison  yeah it's a story we hear way too often  of people mishandling their firearms  and now with the pandemic more and more  people are buying guns without proper  knowledge  of how to handle them  gun safety has always been a huge topic  of discussion  and after this past wednesday's incident  of a mother accidentally killing her  three-year-old son  the need for education when handling and  owning a firearm  is vital in the state of nevada there  are no licenses  mandatory waiting periods or  registrations to purchase firearms  but federal law requires licensed  firearm dealers to run a background  check  on prospective purchasers places like  the range 702 make it their mission to  educate everyone that walks in their  door  on the importance of knowing how to  handle a gun safety classes  and education here for us is exactly and  just as important  as selling a firearm obviously we  believe it's really important to  be able to protect yourself equally it's  just as important to be able to know how  to use that firearm that you're  purchasing  at the range 702 training a potential  buyer is just as important as making a  sale  these are weapons we're dealing with and  even though training isn't required by  law  educating the public is something the  gun store is very passionate about  and prides itself in what we noticed is  there was just a lack of education so we  actually decided to fill that gap  and create one-on-one training classes  where people who  now have the need to have a firearm arm  in their home and  want to protect their family can  actually protect their family because  they know how to use the firearm part of  training also includes the ideal spot  for your weapon when keeping it in the  house  we'll go over where and how to store  your firearm oddly enough it's very  specific  depending on your home depending on your  firearm and depending on who you have in  your home  as for the three-year-old boy and his  mom his mother 25-year-old jasmine  vargas  claims she had no idea there was a round  in the chamber  and while she was legally in possession  of the newly acquired firearm  she told police she had no experience  loading the weapon  and that her boyfriend had loaded it for  her  now the investigation is still ongoing  but this is now a case for metro's abuse  and neglect division  and vargas was booked on a charge of  child abuse with substantial bodily harm  including death reporting live in the  newsroom madison kimbrough  8 news now
 

